1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,868
One menu change can give you almost a quarter more frames per second, and you'll barely see it.

2
00:00:06,618 --> 00:00:11,133
TechSpot tested Cyberpunk 2077 on both presets.

3
00:00:11,413 --> 00:00:15,592
Dropping from Ultra to High gave twenty four percent more frames.

4
00:00:15,872 --> 00:00:19,011
Side by side, the pictures looked almost the same.

5
00:00:19,761 --> 00:00:21,487
So what does Ultra buy you?

6
00:00:21,767 --> 00:00:26,834
In the current version, High mostly trims reflections, fog and crowd size.

7
00:00:27,114 --> 00:00:30,399
You'd spot that in a paused screenshot, not mid fight.

8
00:00:31,149 --> 00:00:32,318
The gain varies.

9
00:00:32,598 --> 00:00:36,189
On that newer version, TechSpot measured fourteen percent.

10
00:00:36,469 --> 00:00:40,415
Games whose presets differ in only a few settings barely change.

11
00:00:41,165 --> 00:00:46,396
So start from High, then raise textures back up if your graphics card has the memory.

12
00:00:47,146 --> 00:00:54,348
We take one PC from 48 frames to the mid 80s in our full video, What Actually Raises FPS.

